sec.p:
The measured phenotypic data were subjected to a statistical analysis using SAS 9.4 (SAS Institute Inc., 2023). The “proc mixed” function was used for the analysis of variance (ANOVA) where treatments were considered fixed effects and environment and block as random effects. The least‐squares means were calculated for FHB and related traits using all replicate data for each environment as well as for the combined dataset. Normality of the dataset was tested using “proc univariate test” and homogeneity of variance for the combined dataset was checked using the “Levene test” in SAS. The correlation between all phenotypic variables was calculated using the “proc corr” function in SAS. Variance components were estimated using “proc var” procedure in SAS, and board‐sense heritability was calculated for each trait using the following equation:
h2=σ2G/(σ2G+σ2GE/E+σ2e/ER);
h 2 is the trait heritability, 𝜎 2 is the variance component, G is the genotypes, E is the environments, GE is the genotype × environment interaction, e is the error variance, and R is the replicates/blocks.
